            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for to sum up, then the Mandarin for a principle you live by."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: fǎnzhèng",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "fǎnzhèng — \"anyway; in any case\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nǐ zuìhǎo bié zháojí fǎnzhèng hái yǒu shíjiān — Try not to worry; there's still time anyway."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "fǎnzhèng is built from fǎn and 正 'proper', both inherited from Middle Chinese, pjonX and tsyengH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to turn over' and the second 'proper'. How the pair came to mean anyway is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons."
